Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.50,0:00:05.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(90,90)}Before investing in solar, one decision connects many questions.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.59,0:00:12.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(90,90)}Is the roof suitable? What could it generate? And how might that investment perform?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.56,0:00:17.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(90,90)}Signix brings those questions into one rooftop planning workspace.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.50,0:00:25.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(90,90)}Begin with a dedicated Home planning experience, using the location and electricity\Ninputs for your scenario.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.50,0:00:34.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(90,90)}The satellite map provides visual context. Draw a planning boundary, then mark the\Nareas you want to exclude.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.93,0:00:41.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(90,90)}Here, a demonstration footprint and obstruction show how usable area changes before\Nsizing begins.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.94,0:00:46.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(90,90)}This is an illustrative planning exercise, not a survey of this building.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.50,0:00:52.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(90,90)}The rooftop designer connects the footprint to a panel layout preview.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.25,0:01:01.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(90,90)}Switch between views and inspect the arrangement. Prototype geometry and unverified\Nshade remain clearly identified.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.50,0:01:09.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(90,90)}Generation forecasts turn the selected system into monthly and long term energy\Nestimates.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.90,0:01:14.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(90,90)}The application exposes its data source and planning assumptions.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.61,0:01:23.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(90,90)}This demonstration uses mock weather fallback. These figures illustrate the\Ncalculation workflow, rather than verified site production.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.50,0:01:33.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(90,90)}For a home, review the estimated investment, household savings, and payback alongside\Nthe assumptions behind them.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.48,0:01:39.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(90,90)}Any residential assistance is indicative and subject to eligibility and official\Nverification.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.57,0:01:43.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(90,90)}A planning estimate is never a guarantee of savings.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.50,0:01:50.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(90,90)}Business planning uses its own commercial policies while sharing the rooftop and\Nenergy workflow.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.80,0:02:00.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(90,90)}Review capital cost, the annual operations and maintenance reserve, net operating\Nbenefit, return on investment, and payback.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.39,0:02:06.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(90,90)}Residential subsidy is not a commercial benefit. Demand charge savings are not\Nmodelled.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.50,0:02:16.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(90,90)}Save a configuration, change one planning choice, and compare the resulting scenarios\Nfor the same roof.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.94,0:02:23.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(90,90)}The side by side view makes differences in capacity, investment, and expected\Nperformance easier to discuss.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.25,0:02:28.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(90,90)}The calculation engine supplies the results shown here.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.50,0:02:34.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(90,90)}Export the planning summary for a conversation with an installer or project partner.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.04,0:02:41.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(90,90)}Keep the assumptions and limitations with the figures, so the next decision starts\Nwith the same context.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.50,0:02:50.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(90,90)}The same report can be explored in English and Hindi, helping more people participate\Nin the decision.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.50,0:03:00.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(90,90)}Map the roof. Understand the energy potential. Compare the investment.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.18,0:03:05.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(90,90)}Signix. Rooftop Solar Planning.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.42,0:03:12.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(90,90)}Use the estimate to ask better questions, then verify the site, design, and approvals\Nbefore procurement.
